1521146.steps:
1. Config DNS Filtering settings(Policy settings, global settings, profile settings, etc.);
2. Sync to Secondary idle.
*Need license on primary and bind two idles in MSW.

1521147.steps:
1. Policy \ Rules and Policies \ DNS Rules, add top: a policy named Test, Interface/Zone-Any, action-Filter, Profile-Default Profile, Enable;
2. Change the action of category 'Gaming' is Block in the Default Profile;
3. Enable 'Enforce DNS Proxy For All DNS Requests' in DNS Proxy page, clear the DNS Cache;
4. In Device &gt; Diagnostics &gt; DNS Name Lookup, DNS Server: System Find location of this URL: www.ea.com.

1521148.steps:
1. Policy \ Rules and Policies \ DNS Rules, add top: a policy named Test, Interface/Zone-Any, action-Filter, Profile-Default Profile, Enable;
2. Change the action of category 'Gaming' is Allow in the Default Profile;
3. Enable 'Enable DNS Sinkhole Service' in DNS Security &gt;DNS Sinkhole page, action is 'Dropping, with Logs';
4. In 'Custom Malicious Domain Name List' tab, add a new entry: www.ea.com;
5. PC connects to X0, set dns server as X0 IP, do dig www.ea.com.

1521149.steps:
1. Policy \ Rules and Policies \ DNS Rules, add top: a policy named Test, Interface/Zone-Any, action-Filter, Profile-Default Profile, Enable;
2. Change the action of category 'Gaming' is Block in the Default Profile;
3. Enable 'Enforce DNS Proxy For All DNS Requests' in DNS Proxy page, clear the DNS Cache;
4. In Address Object, add a FQDN address 'www.ea.com', mouse hovers on the detail of the entry;
5. Select it and click Resolve selected; 6. Mouse hovers on 'www.ea.com'.

1521150.steps:
1. Policy \ Rules and Policies \ DNS Rules, add top: a policy named Test, Interface/Zone-Any, action-Filter, Profile-Default Profile, Enable;
2. Change the action of category 'Gaming' is Block in the Default Profile;
3. Enable 'Enforce DNS Proxy For All DNS Requests' in DNS Proxy page, clear the DNS Cache;
4. In Device &gt; Diagnostics &gt; Ping, Ping host or IP address: www.ea.com.

1521151.steps:
1. Policy \ Rules and Policies \ DNS Rules, add top: a policy named Test, Interface-X0, action-Filter, Profile-Default Profile, Enable;
2. Change the action of category 'Gaming' is Block in the Default Profile;
3. Enable 'Enable proxying of split DNS servers' in DNS Proxy page;
4. In Split DNS tab, add a new entry: IP Version: IPv4, Domain Name: www.ea.com, IPv4 DNS Server Primary: 10.190.202.200, Local Interface: X0;
5. PC connects to X0, set dns server as X0 IP, do' dig www.ea.com'.

1521187.steps:
1. Make sure DNS Security license is activated;
2. DNS Security \ Settings \ DNS Filtering tab and DNS Security \ Reports page, check the page;
3. From GUI and CLI, enter configure mode, add a dns policy with action-Filter.

1521188.steps:
1. Make sure DNS Security license is NOT activated;
2. <span>DNS Security \ Settings \ DNS Filtering tab and DNS Security \ Reports page, check the page</span>;
3. From GUI and CLI, enter configure mode, add a dns policy with action-Filter.

1521189.steps:
1.Device &gt; Log &gt; Settings, enable DNS Filtering Expiration Message, set its log priority to alert and display interval to 0;
2.Add a dns filter policy from X0, with default profile;
3.Make DNS Filtering license expired, check the logs;
4.DNS Security \ Settings \ DNS Filtering tab and DNS Security \ Reports page, check the pages;
5.From GUI and CLI, enter configure mode, add/edit a dns policy with action-Filter.
6.From LAN client, dig adult.com @X0-ip,(domain should with negative reply) check the result
